                        Step 2: Understand the problem

The data.txt file contains many lines of words and passwords.

Our goal is to find the line containing the word:

millionth

Instead of manually searching through all the lines, we can use the grep command.

                          Step 3: Search for the required word

Use:

cat data.txt | grep 'millionth'

In the screenshot, this command successfully finds the line containing millionth.

                            Step 4: Understand the command
cat data.txt
cat data.txt

cat displays the contents of data.txt.

| — Pipe
|

The pipe sends the output of the cat command to the next command.

grep 'millionth'
grep 'millionth'

grep searches the incoming text for the word millionth.

So:

cat data.txt | grep 'millionth'

means:

Display the contents of data.txt and search for the line containing millionth.

                         Step 5: Identify the result

